Z||000000||Sootah||07-15-2001||07:18 PM||||My cat has plugged. Started it up this morning and it was runnung reeealy weak, I went to my fathers house and left it idling when I went in, I came back out and saw smoke coming out from under the car. I turned it off really quickly and looked under the car. My car was GLOWING in the middle. The strange thing is that I drove home last night (114 miles) and it ran fine the whole way, even as I pulled into the garage. Any ideas?<P>PS: I already know what I am going to do. There is no emmisions testing around here, so I am gonna make it a 'high-flow' cat.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Never argue with an idiot, they drag you down to their level and then beat you with experience||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||07-15-2001||07:25 PM||||bad tuning, bad gas, or just normal wear n tear are usually the reasons. remember if its original its been on almost 20 years. If I remember right, if its got less than something like 60k or 100k isnt any emmissions parts supposed to be replaced for free???? just a thought. I know my Lincoln limo had 160K and the local dealer installed 2 new ones for free on it.||||reg||1
